 "reports_individuals_with_tnfaip3_variant": true,
 "relevance_note": "A narrative review of neutrophil defects in periodontitis that gives individual-level detail for a few LAD-I patients, e.g. \"our patient was a 19-year-old male with moderate LAD-I disease\" (previously published, ref 59) and the Figure 3 legend \"a 15-year-old male with LAD-I\".",
 "method_note": "Read the whole review by hand; JSON assembled by a short Python script from hand-chosen values and spans; no table transcription (the paper has no data tables). Three in-scope people: (1) the ustekinumab-treated patient previously published as ref 59 (label 'ref 59 patient', source_reference_in_review '59'); (2) the 15-year-old male in the Figure 3A legend ('unnamed person 1'); (3) the LAD-I patient whose extracted tooth is shown in Figure 3B ('unnamed person 2'). The paper does not say whether the Figure 3A and 3B people are the same person, or whether either is the ref 59 patient (who was 19 years old); they are kept as separate rows and not merged. The Figure 3 people are not stated to be previously published, so source_reference_in_review is 'not reported'. No ITGB2 variant is printed or tied to any individual (only the general statement that LAD-I results from mutations in ITGB2), so the variants table is empty. is_proband left null (review, no proband/index wording). Age 19 and 15 recorded as age at last evaluation (age at the described treatment / radiograph). Figure 3 title 'Severe periodontitis in leukocyte adhesion deficiency I' was not used to set the periodontitis checklist item for the Figure 3B person; that person's bone destruction is recorded only as phenotypic_features rows. Ref 59 patient's 'deep cutaneous ulcer' is not stated to be necrotic, so the necrotic-ulcer checklist item is 'not reported'. Group-level statements (e.g. periodontal disease in >50% of cases, ref 54) were not attributed to anyone. No contradictions found.",
